      "a": "wer:\nA candle\nIII. You are asked to create a magical object. What object would you create? Make a drawing with all its details and mention its special quality on the same sheet. Put up the sheet on the display board.\nAnswer:\nObject Name:\nGlowSphere\nDrawing Suggestion:\nA glowing crystal ball with stars and swirling mist inside.\nSpecial Quality:\nThe GlowSphere grants one wish each day\u2014but only if the wish is kind and helps someone else. It shines even brighter every time a good deed is done.\nMastering The Magic Brush of Dreams: Key Concepts & NCERT Solutions\nThe chapter\nMagic Brush of Dreams\nfrom Class 8 English Poorvi delivers inspiring lessons on compassion and responsibility. By working through detailed NCERT solutions, students develop a clear understanding of the poem\u2019s sequence and symbolism, ensuring strong exam preparation and improved comprehension skills.\nRegular practice with these\nNCERT question answers for Class 8 English Chapter 8\nbuilds confidence and strengthens analytical thinking. Students should focus on the significance of key events and characters\u2019 motives, as questions often revolve around moral values and poetic techniques discussed in this chapter.\nConsistent revision and a clear grasp of the\nMCQs, match the following, and creative essay sections\nwill help you score higher. Always read the poem thoroughly, break down questions, and review answers for a strong performance in your Class 8 English exams."
