      "a": "wer:\nDo it yourself\nII. Some microplanktons in the sea are bioluminescent. Have you seen any other life form that has this quality? Identify the insect given below and find out what it is called in your language. Look out for it when you visit a field or a place with a wetland.\nAnswer:\nInsect Shown:\nFirefly\nBioluminescence:\nFireflies emit light from their abdomen through a chemical reaction, similar to the glow produced by microplanktons.\nCommon Names in Indian Languages:\nHindi:\nJugnu\nMalayalam:\nMinnaminungu\nTamil:\nMinnal Poochi\nBengali:\nJonaki Poka\nTelugu:\nDeepa Purugu\nMarathi:\nJugas\nThe Case of the Fifth Word \u2013 NCERT Solutions Class 8 English Poorvi Chapter 9 (2026-27)\nExploring\nThe Case of the Fifth Word\nin Class 8 English Poorvi helps students strengthen analytical and reasoning skills. Using\nchapter-wise NCERT solutions\nmakes understanding story clues and character motivations simpler, ensuring a solid grasp of the content for exams.\nIn the 2026-27 NCERT curriculum, mastering each story\u2019s nuances and tackling exercises is vital. Practicing with\ndirect answers\nand reviewing\nfactual explanations\nhelps you ace tests with confidence. Focus on understanding patterns and hidden messages in passages for better results.\nStay consistent with your practice, revisit\nNCERT Class 8 English Chapter 9\nregularly, and pay attention to every exercise. This approach strengthens language skills and prepares you to score more in the board exam and other assessments."
